<section id="s-efficiency" data-code="efficiency">
<div class="section-no">05 — 7,000× Fewer Tokens</div>
<h2>The Pareto Frontier of AR-to-Diffusion Conversion</h2>
<p>
  The headline result is the token efficiency. Every other ARLM-to-DLM conversion
  method requires billions to trillions of tokens. OPDLM needs only 66–76 million —
  roughly the size of a fine-tuning run, not a pretraining run.
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">AIME-24 accuracy vs. training tokens — log scale</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">OPDLM sits at the Pareto frontier</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <canvas id="efficiency-canvas" style="width:100%;height:280px;display:block"></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

<p>
  The chart above mirrors Figure 1 from the paper. <strong>OPDLM-8B reaches 14.7%
  on AIME-24 using only 0.066B tokens</strong> — while LLaDA-8B needed 1,500B tokens
  to reach just 2.1%, and Dream-7B used 580B tokens to reach 0.0% on the same
  benchmark. Even the strongest baseline, Fast-dLLM-v2, used 15× more tokens for
  comparable accuracy.
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">token comparison — 8B scale</span>
  </div>
